To build an agent with the `create_agent` factory you import the function and call it, providing the model you want to use and the list of tools (and optionally a `system_prompt`). For example:

```python
from langchain.agents import create_agent

agent = create_agent(
    model="claude-sonnet-4-6",
    tools=[search_web, analyze_data, send_email],
    system_prompt="You are a helpful research assistant."
)

result = agent.invoke({
    "messages": [
        {"role": "user", "content": "Research AI safety trends"}
    ]
})
```

The function returns a compiled LangGraph graph that you can invoke with `agent.invoke`. [Source: https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/migrate/langchain-v1]

